# Netlify redirects. This file has to sit in the root of the publish
# directory, which for this site is the repo root, since there is no
# build step.
#
# ---- .html -> the canonical extension-less URL ----------------------
#
# Every page below carries a rel=canonical and hreflang pointing at the
# extension-less form of its own URL. These rules make the .html path
# agree with those tags instead of quietly serving a second copy of the
# same page at a second address.
#
# The "!" is required rather than decorative. A plain 301 is ignored
# whenever a real file sits at the requested path, and every one of
# these .html files does exist in the publish directory, so without the
# force flag Netlify would serve the file and the rule would never fire.
#
# thanks.html and thanks-th.html are deliberately absent. Both
# reservation forms POST to those exact paths (the action attribute on
# the form in reservation.html and reservation-th.html). A forced
# redirect there risks catching the POST before Netlify's form handler
# sees it, which turns the submission into a GET and loses the booking.
# Those two pages are noindex, so there is nothing to gain by
# redirecting them.

/index.html             /                  301!
/index-th.html          /index-th          301!
/loykrathong.html       /loykrathong       301!
/loykrathong-th.html    /loykrathong-th    301!
/reservation.html       /reservation       301!
/reservation-th.html    /reservation-th    301!
